{"files":[{"content":"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing ll = long long;\n\nstatic int A[1000][1000];\nstatic int transposed[1000][1000];\n\nclass FrequencyTable {\n  vector<ll> keys;\n  vector<ll> counts;\n  vector<uint32_t> generations;\n  size_t mask;\n  uint32_t generation = 0;\n\n  static uint64_t hash_key(ll key) {\n    uint64_t x = static_cast<uint64_t>(key) + 0x9e3779b97f4a7c15ULL;\n    x = (x ^ (x >> 30)) * 0xbf58476d1ce4e5b9ULL;\n    x = (x ^ (x >> 27)) * 0x94d049bb133111ebULL;\n    return x ^ (x >> 31);\n  }\n\npublic:\n  explicit FrequencyTable(int max_prefix_length) {\n    size_t capacity = 1;\n    const size_t needed = 2 * (static_cast<size_t>(max_prefix_length) + 1);\n    while (capacity < needed)\n      capacity <<= 1;\n    keys.resize(capacity);\n    counts.resize(capacity);\n    generations.resize(capacity);\n    mask = capacity - 1;\n  }\n\n  void reset() {\n    ++generation;\n    if (generation == 0) {\n      fill(generations.begin(), generations.end(), 0);\n      generation = 1;\n    }\n  }\n\n  ll count(ll key) const {\n    size_t slot = hash_key(key) & mask;\n    while (generations[slot] == generation) {\n      if (keys[slot] == key)\n        return counts[slot];\n      slot = (slot + 1) & mask;\n    }\n    return 0;\n  }\n\n  void increment(ll key) {\n    size_t slot = hash_key(key) & mask;\n    while (generations[slot] == generation) {\n      if (keys[slot] == key) {\n        ++counts[slot];\n        return;\n      }\n      slot = (slot + 1) & mask;\n    }\n    generations[slot] = generation;\n    keys[slot] = key;\n    counts[slot] = 1;\n  }\n};\n\nll solve(int m, int n, ll k) {\n  const bool transpose_matrix = m > n;\n  const int small = min(m, n);\n  const int longer = max(m, n);\n  int (*work)[1000] = A;\n\n  if (transpose_matrix) {\n    for (int row = 0; row < n; ++row)\n      for (int col = 0; col < m; ++col)\n        transposed[row][col] = A[col][row];\n    work = transposed;\n  }\n\n  ll ans = 0;\n#pragma omp parallel if((ll)small * (small + 1) / 2 * longer >= 32768) reduction(+ : ans)\n  {\n    FrequencyTable frequencies(longer);\n    vector<ll> compressed(longer);\n\n#pragma omp for schedule(dynamic, 1)\n    for (int top = 0; top < small; ++top) {\n      fill(compressed.begin(), compressed.end(), 0);\n      for (int bottom = top; bottom < small; ++bottom) {\n        for (int col = 0; col < longer; ++col)\n          compressed[col] += work[bottom][col];\n\n        frequencies.reset();\n        frequencies.increment(0);\n        ll prefix = 0;\n        for (int col = 0; col < longer; ++col) {\n          prefix += compressed[col];\n          ans += frequencies.count(prefix - k);\n          frequencies.increment(prefix);\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n  ll k;\n  int m, n;\n  if (!(cin >> k >> m >> n))\n    return 0;\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i)\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n      cin >> A[i][j];\n\n  cout << solve(m, n, k) << '\\n';\n  return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/main.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"Pairing along the smaller matrix dimension reduces the scan work, while a reusable per-thread frequency table and parallel work sharing reduce hashing and serial execution costs without assumptions about matrix values.","notes":"The OpenMP pragmas require an OpenMP-enabled build to use multiple threads; otherwise they are ignored and the implementation remains serial and correct. No commands were run.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Compress each row/column band along the shorter dimension, transposing tall matrices so the scan remains contiguous; complexity is O(min(m,n)^2 * max(m,n)).","Replace per-band unordered_map operations with a bounded, power-of-two open-addressed table using signed 64-bit keys/counts and generation stamps for reuse.","Work-share independent band starts with dynamic scheduling and a 64-bit reduction; use a generic work threshold to avoid parallel overhead on small inputs."]}